        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Is it really a cop-out? It seems the reasonable choice for UIs that want to show an actual tab selection UI-widget, and not \"a first reserved line of the screen grid, which by default is used for tabs but also can be used for other random stuff\". I'm not saying the later is bad and shouldn't be externalized. Just that `guitablabel` has a purpose on its own to fulfill a common set of expectations (one text label per real tabpage) for some UIs that `tabline` cannot be guaranteed to fulfill. It also best fits the current `tabline_update` event, which exports an array of tabs, not an array of tabline text chunks.\r\n",
            "created_at": "2018-01-21T17:57:45Z",
